    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A loose union of princes, bishops and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city">free cities</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, under an elected emperor from 962 to 1806.</li><li>Its fragmentation let the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> survive and produced religious settlements that shaped the modern idea of state <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> made the title meaningless, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> quietly dissolved the empire in 1806.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The empire had no standing army for most of its history; its military strength depended on contingents the princes sent only when politically willing.</p></aside>
    </section>

